1
00:00:01,100 --> 00:00:02,913
Pyre. Coins that build apps.

2
00:00:04,950 --> 00:00:07,618
Write one sentence. An agent writes the spec.

3
00:00:07,838 --> 00:00:12,100
Stake 0.05 ETH, refundable, and it launches on pons.

4
00:00:15,500 --> 00:00:18,774
70% of every trade fee comes back:

5
00:00:18,994 --> 00:00:24,023
60 to the build budget, 25 to a PYRE buyback, 15 to the launcher.

6
00:00:27,623 --> 00:00:30,617
At $50, an agent builds in a sandbox.

7
00:00:30,837 --> 00:00:34,848
Nothing deploys until the build, Lighthouse and a reviewer pass.

8
00:00:35,648 --> 00:00:40,485
It goes live on its own subdomain, free to use. Holders unlock features.

9
00:00:41,285 --> 00:00:43,602
A quarter of every fee buys PYRE.

10
00:00:47,485 --> 00:00:49,515
Then it burns. Supply falls.

11
00:00:49,735 --> 00:00:53,043
Every burn carries an attestation anyone can reproduce.

12
00:00:57,485 --> 00:01:00,733
No budget, no agent. Any new fee relights it.

13
00:01:01,685 --> 00:01:06,581
Every test, every audit and an independent security review, in the public repo.

14
00:01:07,935 --> 00:01:09,745
Pyre. Live on Robinhood Chain.

